# Bytes as committed, on every platform. README.md is deliberately CRLF
# (scripts/check_line_endings.py guards it) and every translation records
# the SHA-256 of its source (scripts/check_translations.py); a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would rewrite both and turn every
# translation check red. Conversion is switched off wholesale rather than
# per file so a new text file cannot fall through the gaps.
* -text
